---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Image from '../../components/OptimizedImage.astro';
import gabeImage from '../../../assets/gabe_whisnant_1.webp';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Class of '96 Spotlight: Gabe Whisnant, from The Shelby Star to Newsweek | Community Spotlight"
  description="From Crest High Class of '96 to The Shelby Star and now Newsweek, meet Gabe Whisnant — a dedicated journalist keeping the stories that matter alive."
>
  <article class="pt-32 pb-24 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <header class="mb-16 text-center">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 mb-6 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-orange-500/20 bg-orange-500/5">
          <span class="text-orange-500 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">Community Spotlight</span>
          <span class="w-1 h-1 rounded-full bg-orange-500/30"></span>
          <span class="text-brand-sky/60 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest">August 2026</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-heading text-5xl md:text-7xl font-black text-white mb-8 tracking-tight leading-[1.1]">
          Class of '96 Spotlight: <br />
          <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-cyan to-brand-blue">Gabe Whisnant, from The Shelby Star to Newsweek</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-brand-sky/80 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mx-auto italic">
          A personal reflection from a fellow Crest High Class of 1996 graduate.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-none">
        <p class="text-brand-sky/80 mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          In the Class of 1996 at Crest High School, we all had big dreams. Some of us went into business, healthcare, teaching, or trades. My friend Gabe Whisnant took a different path, one that would keep him deeply connected to the heartbeat of Shelby and Cleveland County for decades.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-12 leading-relaxed">
          Today, Gabe serves as a News Editor at <a href="https://www.newsweek.com/authors/gabe-whisnant" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline decoration-brand-cyan/30 underline-offset-4">Newsweek</a>, based right here in North Carolina — a long way from where his story started, yet still rooted in the values of honest, community-focused journalism.
        </p>

        <div class="my-12 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl max-w-[640px] mx-auto">
          <Image src={gabeImage} alt="Gabe Whisnant, Shelby Star and Newsweek journalist" class="w-full h-auto" />
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">A Local Kid Who Never Left the Story</h2>
        <p class="text-brand-sky/80 mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Born and raised in Cleveland County, Gabe graduated from Crest High in 1996. Like many of us, he carried a strong sense of place with him. After starting his journalism career at the Goldsboro News-Argus, he returned home in 2006 as a sports reporter for The Shelby Star. He later served as sports editor for The Star and its sister paper, The Gaston Gazette, before moving into news leadership roles.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Whether covering Friday night lights, high school state championships, or the personal stories behind the athletes, Gabe has always understood that local sports are more than scores, they are about community pride, character, and connection.
        </p>

        <p class="text-brand-sky/80 mb-12 leading-relaxed">
          Even as his career took him into digital leadership and larger roles, including time as news editor at The Star and later executive positions across the Carolinas, his roots in Shelby have remained strong. As an executive editor, Gabe led award-winning coverage of major stories — including the 2015 capture of Charleston church shooter Dylann Roof and the Alex Murdaugh double murder case. Prior to joining Newsweek in 2023, he directed daily publications across North and South Carolina.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">Why Local Journalism Still Matters in 2026</h2>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          In an era dominated by national news feeds and social media highlights, outlets like The Shelby Star remain essential. Gabe and his colleagues have spent years chronicling the triumphs, challenges, and everyday heroes of Cleveland County.
        </p>

        <ul class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 list-none p-0 mb-12">
          <li class="bg-brand-dark/30 p-4 rounded-xl border border-white/5 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="text-orange-500">✦</span><span class="text-brand-sky/80">It connects neighbors through shared stories</span></li>
          <li class="bg-brand-dark/30 p-4 rounded-xl border border-white/5 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="text-orange-500">✦</span><span class="text-brand-sky/80">It celebrates young athletes and coaches</span></li>
          <li class="bg-brand-dark/30 p-4 rounded-xl border border-white/5 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="text-orange-500">✦</span><span class="text-brand-sky/80">It reflects the good and the areas needing attention</span></li>
          <li class="bg-brand-dark/30 p-4 rounded-xl border border-white/5 flex items-center gap-3"><span class="text-orange-500">✦</span><span class="text-brand-sky/80">It preserves small-town sports history national outlets miss</span></li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-brand-sky/80 mb-12 leading-relaxed">
          This kind of community storytelling builds the social fabric that makes Shelby and surrounding areas special.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">How Digital Tools Are Helping Local Media Thrive</h2>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Here is where the conversation gets exciting for those of us in the digital space. As a web agency owner helping local businesses grow online, I have seen firsthand how modern websites, SEO, and digital strategies are giving institutions like The Shelby Star new life.
        </p>

        <ul class="space-y-3 text-brand-sky/80 mb-12">
          <li>• Reach readers on mobile devices, where most people consume news today</li>
          <li>• Deliver stories faster with richer media like photos, video, and interactive features</li>
          <li>• Improve visibility in Google for searches like Shelby High football scores and Crest High athletics</li>
          <li>• Build sustainable revenue through stronger user experience and engagement</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-brand-sky/80 mb-12 leading-relaxed">
          The best local journalists, like Gabe, blend old-school reporting instincts with a modern digital mindset. That balance keeps traditional media relevant and impactful in 2026.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">A Class of '96 Connection</h2>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          It has been fun watching Gabe's journey from the sidelines at Crest High, to the press box at The Shelby Star, and now to the national news desk at Newsweek. His commitment to honest, community-focused journalism is something our entire graduating class can be proud of.
        </p>

        <p class="text-brand-sky/80 mb-12 leading-relaxed">
          To read some of his past work covering Shelby and Cleveland County sports and news, visit <a href="https://www.shelbystar.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline decoration-brand-cyan/30 underline-offset-4">The Shelby Star website</a>. Many of his bylines from his time there still resonate with locals today. And to follow his current work, check out his <a href="https://www.newsweek.com/authors/gabe-whisnant" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline decoration-brand-cyan/30 underline-offset-4">author page at Newsweek</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">Here's to the Storytellers</h2>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          In a fast-changing world, people like Gabe Whisnant remind us why local voices matter. They keep the spirit of Shelby sports, and Shelby itself, alive for the next generation.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-orange-600 to-brand-darkest p-10 rounded-[2rem] text-center relative overflow-hidden my-12">
          <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_50%_50%,rgba(255,165,0,0.1),transparent_70%)]"></div>
          <p class="text-white text-xl md:text-2xl font-medium relative z-10">
            To my friend and fellow Class of '96 grad: thank you for the stories you've told and the community you've helped strengthen.
          </p>
          <p class="text-orange-200 mt-4 relative z-10">
            Oh and one more thing Gabe. You ready? Here goes... ch ch ch CHEEECKEN! Lol.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 p-8 bg-brand-dark/50 border border-white/5 rounded-2xl">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">More Community Spotlights</h2>
        <div class="space-y-2 text-brand-sky/70">
          <p>Read more about the people and businesses keeping our region strong: <a href="/blog/newtons-karate-jimmy-newton-spotlight/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">Jimmy Newton of Newton's Karate</a>, <a href="/blog/daniel-thomas-mayor-boiling-springs-spotlight/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">Mayor Daniel Thomas of Boiling Springs</a>, and <a href="/blog/fs-expedited-llc-spotlight/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">F&amp;S Expedited LLC</a>.</p>
          <p class="mt-4">Love seeing local businesses thrive? We spotlight Cleveland County companies through our <a href="/services/web-design/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">web design</a> and <a href="/services/seo/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">local SEO</a> services.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <footer class="mt-24 pt-12 border-t border-white/5 flex flex-wrap gap-8 items-center justify-between">
        <a href="/blog/" class="text-brand-sky/60 hover:text-white transition-colors flex items-center gap-2">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/></svg>
          Back to Blog
        </a>
        <div class="flex gap-6">
          <a href="/" class="text-brand-sky/60 hover:text-white transition-colors">Home</a>
          <a href="/about/" class="text-brand-sky/60 hover:text-white transition-colors">About Us</a>
          <a href="/contact/" class="text-brand-sky/60 hover:text-white transition-colors">Contact</a>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
